Parts with their own terms:

- The chart engine, @zodiacs/engine, is MIT AND CC-BY-4.0: its code is MIT,
  and its ΔT module carries 32 values of Table S15 of Stephenson, Morrison
  and Hohenkerk (2016) under CC BY 4.0, as its NOTICE says. It also carries
  time data (the IANA time zone history before 1970 and the IERS leap-second
  list, both public domain, and a UT1 − UTC table derived from IERS series)
  and catalogue values for the stars of its Vedic ayanamsas; its NOTICE names
  each source, and its LICENSING.md gives the terms and three questions about
  them that are still open. Its source is at
  https://github.com/zodiacs-org/engine, and the archive in vendor/ carries
  its own licence files.
- The shared sky data the site publishes under /api/v1/ is licensed under
  CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
- Place names and coordinates are from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/),
  licensed under CC BY 4.0 and converted into the site's own format.
- Third-party packages keep their own licences.
